.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap95/review_pass1.log:3280:The core sticky override can be bypassed by later mapper modes, so the new stmap95 policy does not reliably enforce its intended protection. The diagnostics also misreport sticky-blocked candidates.
.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap95/review_pass1.log:3288:  In the sticky-block path the branch was entered only because `fAccepted` was true, but clearing `fAccepted` here is what the later diagnostic `accepted-before` field prints, so every `sticky-block-replacement` row reports `accepted-before = 0`. That makes the CSV/logs hide that the sticky policy vetoed a cut selected by the previous comparator; keep a separate pre-veto value for diagnostics before clearing the selection.
