codex
The sticky policy can be bypassed by replacements accepted through the emitted-drive override path, so the main behavioral change is not fully enforced. The tracked campaign state also appears to be left in an active/prepared state.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Apply sticky veto to emitted-drive overrides — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:1908-1908
  When a later target-phase cut is not selected by the earlier comparator but this same hook would accept it as an emitted-drive override, `fAccepted` is false here so the sticky check is skipped; the branch below can still set `fAccepted = 1` and replace the sticky cut without the >2 ps / drive-preservation test. This means stmap95 does not enforce its sticky policy for override-driven replacements.

- [P2] Clear active campaign state before committing — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/.autoeda/runtime/campaign_state.json:9-11
  With the stmap95 implementation and validation artifacts present, this tracked state now says iteration 95 is still `iteration-prepared` and active while `completed_iterations` is already 95 and `last_completed_iteration` remains 94. Any resume/launcher logic reading the checked-in state can treat stmap95 as still in progress instead of advancing, so this should be finalized or cleared before the patch lands.
